# Crusader (RX26) udev rules — stable device names + permissions.
# Install with install_udev.sh.
#
# Only the devices ACTUALLY ABOARD get a rule. A symlink for hardware that is not
# on the boat is worse than no symlink: it makes a config file look satisfied
# while pointing at whatever else happened to enumerate. Confirmed aboard
# 2026-07-28 (docs/OPERATIONS.md); a Teensy (16c0:0483) and a Prolific PL2303
# (067b:23a3) also enumerate and deliberately get NO rule until someone traces
# the cable.
#
# Discover attrs for a plugged-in device:
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -E 'idVendor|idProduct|serial' | head

# --- Pixhawk (autopilot). Owned exclusively by MAVProxy; everything else uses the
#     rebroadcast. The symlink exists so crsd-mavproxy.service never chases ttyACM
#     numbering.
#     5741 is what Crusader's board actually enumerates as (confirmed on the
#     Jetson: usb-ArduPilot_Pixhawk1_3A001F00...). The other IDs cover the boards
#     we might swap in: 5740 other ArduPilot/Holybro, 26ac 3DR, 2dae CubePilot.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1209", ATTRS{idProduct}=="5741", SYMLINK+="crsd-pixhawk", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1209", ATTRS{idProduct}=="5740", SYMLINK+="crsd-pixhawk", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="26ac", SYMLINK+="crsd-pixhawk", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2dae", SYMLINK+="crsd-pixhawk", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"

# --- LED Arduino (led_node's serial target; its auto-reconnect expects a stable
#     path). Crusader's board is a CH340 clone with NO SERIAL NUMBER, which is
#     why a second CH340 must never go aboard: the two would be indistinguishable
#     and the symlink would land on whichever enumerated first.
#     2341 = genuine Arduino, kept for a board swap.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="crsd-led", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2341", SYMLINK+="crsd-led", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"

# --- 915MHz telemetry radio (SiK, Silabs CP210x). Optional: the boat flies
#     without it (the 5.8GHz link carries telemetry), so install_udev.sh does not
#     warn when it is absent.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", SYMLINK+="crsd-telem", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"

# --- OAK-D LR (Luxonis / Intel Movidius). NOT this stack's device — the camera
#     runs in its own container — but udev rules are a property of the HOST, and
#     this one only grants access permissions (no symlink, nothing here opens it).
#     It stays so that removing it from this repo does not silently break the
#     camera container on a shared Jetson. Move it to that container's own
#     installer when it grows one, and delete these three lines.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="03e7", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev"
